WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.320 --> 00:00:04.760
Actor Tom Hardy often portrays characters
that are dangerous, cold, and calculating.

00:00:04.760 --> 00:00:08.559
That makes him the perfect choice to play
Venom, the slimy antihero at the center of

00:00:08.560 --> 00:00:10.000
Marvel's Spider-Man spinoff.

00:00:11.620 --> 00:00:14.020
"We are Venom."

00:00:15.020 --> 00:00:18.920
Hardy seems to have the ability to physically
transform himself for any role.

00:00:18.920 --> 00:00:23.289
Here's a rundown of his most remarkable transformations
over the years, all of which helped him get

00:00:23.289 --> 00:00:25.200
the physique necessary to play Venom.

00:00:25.480 --> 00:00:26.860
Dropping weight for Stuart

00:00:27.580 --> 00:00:29.560
Tom Hardy is far from a natural athlete.

00:00:29.860 --> 00:00:34.120
He's admitted to feeling "small and skinny
and vulnerable" as a child, and was intimidated

00:00:34.120 --> 00:00:35.980
by the gym because of all the testosterone.

00:00:36.710 --> 00:00:41.780
His first dedicated physical transformation
began with the 2007 biopic, Stuart: A Life

00:00:41.780 --> 00:00:42.280
Backwards.

00:00:42.660 --> 00:00:46.800
Hardy lost a whole lot of weight to portray
Stuart Shorter, a homeless heroin addict with

00:00:46.800 --> 00:00:48.060
muscular dystrophy.

00:00:48.329 --> 00:00:52.160
He lost almost 30 pounds for the role, but
took a relatively healthy approach to his

00:00:52.160 --> 00:00:53.360
body transformation.

00:00:53.640 --> 00:00:57.560
Hardy worked with a personal trainer, ran
several miles a day, and kept a diet rich

00:00:57.560 --> 00:01:01.380
in protein… including eating as as much
spinach and greens as he wanted.

00:01:05.200 --> 00:01:09.600
Fortunately for his sanity, the training and
diet regimen only lasted five or six weeks.

00:01:10.100 --> 00:01:11.160
Bulking up for Bronson

00:01:11.700 --> 00:01:16.680
When he began training for the lead role in
Bronson, Hardy needed to pack on serious weight.

00:01:16.689 --> 00:01:18.000
He told I Love Film:

00:01:18.000 --> 00:01:22.540
"I probably weighed about 11 stone with, like,
drenched, with stones in my pocket.”

00:01:22.640 --> 00:01:26.780
To play the notoriously violent criminal,
Hardy only had five weeks to bulk up.

00:01:27.060 --> 00:01:31.350
Using a bare-bones workout routine, Hardy
managed to miraculously put on seven pounds

00:01:31.350 --> 00:01:31.840
a week.

00:01:31.880 --> 00:01:37.320
His trainer, ex-Marine Patrick "Pnut"Monroe,
added lots of variation to his workouts, making

00:01:37.320 --> 00:01:39.320
every rep difficult in one way or another.

00:01:39.840 --> 00:01:45.620
"We had to develop a solitary physique; the
kind of physique you would develop if you

00:01:45.620 --> 00:01:49.020
only had four walls and a floor."

00:01:49.620 --> 00:01:51.380
Upping intensity for Warrior

00:01:52.000 --> 00:01:57.160
For his next film Warrior, Tom Hardy demonstrated
impressive discipline while preparing for

00:01:57.160 --> 00:01:59.340
his role as a Marine turned MMA fighter.

00:02:00.020 --> 00:02:05.060
Hardy packed on slabs of lean muscle to convincingly
portray a professional athlete, and his daily

00:02:05.060 --> 00:02:06.500
training regimen was tough.

00:02:06.640 --> 00:02:10.800
He even lifted weights with his teeth to build
neck muscles… you heard that right.

00:02:11.500 --> 00:02:16.820
"It was like two hours two hours boxing, two
hours kickboxing, two hours of Muay Thai,

00:02:16.820 --> 00:02:20.120
then two hours choreography a day, and then
two hours lifting, every day."

00:02:20.250 --> 00:02:25.300
The actor ate five or six high-protein meals
per day, and wound up 29 pounds heavier than

00:02:25.300 --> 00:02:26.420
when he trained for Bronson.

00:02:27.060 --> 00:02:28.140
Beefing up for Bane

00:02:28.780 --> 00:02:33.030
To play the masked villain Bane in The Dark
Knight Rises, Hardy needed to appear larger

00:02:33.030 --> 00:02:35.860
than life, which he achieved by packing on
even more size.

00:02:36.550 --> 00:02:40.640
Prior to shooting, Hardy appeared on Chatty
Man and opened up about the physical demands

00:02:40.640 --> 00:02:41.140
of the role:

00:02:41.340 --> 00:02:45.120
"I'm gonna have to get up to about thirteen
and a half, fourteen stone… and I'm twelve

00:02:45.120 --> 00:02:48.220
and a bit now, so I've got three months to
do that."

00:02:48.220 --> 00:02:49.220
"How'd you bulk up?!"

00:02:49.220 --> 00:02:50.220
"Fat.

00:02:50.220 --> 00:02:51.080
A lot of fat."

00:02:51.220 --> 00:02:55.560
Packing on 30 pounds brought Hardy's weight
up considerably: He was almost 200 pounds

00:02:55.560 --> 00:02:56.780
by the time filming began.

00:02:57.240 --> 00:03:01.820
But as he told Jonathan Ross, that still wasn't
enough to intimidate Christian Bale on the

00:03:01.820 --> 00:03:02.620
first day of shooting:

00:03:02.880 --> 00:03:09.640
"And I looked at him and he was looking at
me like, 'Oh yeah, I'm Batman.'"

00:03:11.620 --> 00:03:12.660
Losing mass for Max

00:03:13.260 --> 00:03:18.350
In order to play the title character in Mad
Max: Fury Road, Hardy had to lose thirty pounds…

00:03:18.350 --> 00:03:20.560
the same amount of weight he gained to play
Bane.

00:03:21.070 --> 00:03:23.780
He told Collider he wanted to look like "a
hungry wolf.

00:03:23.780 --> 00:03:25.360
Or like when you put a cat in the bath."

00:03:25.920 --> 00:03:30.410
Hardy reached his goal in a surprising way:
by smoking cigarettes and eating only one

00:03:30.410 --> 00:03:31.180
meal per day.

00:03:31.620 --> 00:03:35.060
Once the weight was dropped, the next step
was three or four months of fight training.

00:03:35.580 --> 00:03:38.780
Hardy didn't exactly have time to rest when
cameras were rolling, either.

00:03:39.340 --> 00:03:40.440
He told Men's Fitness:

00:03:40.720 --> 00:03:44.380
"It's a very physical shoot from the beginning,
from the training right through to the six

00:03:44.380 --> 00:03:45.700
months of shooting on the ground."

00:03:46.300 --> 00:03:47.660
Finding his inner Venom

00:03:48.090 --> 00:03:53.400
By the time Venom started filming in October
2017, Hardy was already a master at transforming

00:03:53.400 --> 00:03:53.900
his body.

00:03:54.410 --> 00:03:58.000
He got ripped for the role by applying tools
he'd accumulated over years of hard work,

00:03:58.000 --> 00:03:59.980
with no quick fix or magic ingredient.

00:04:00.180 --> 00:04:04.200
He required guidance from professional MMA
fighter Nathan Jones and personal trainer

00:04:04.200 --> 00:04:08.080
Mark Mene, and trained in a combination of
boxing, MMA, and kickboxing.

00:04:08.360 --> 00:04:12.180
"He's a good student -- receptive, open to
learning."

00:04:12.500 --> 00:04:16.510
Judging from a sparring video Jones posted
on Instagram, Hardy adapted to the challenge

00:04:16.510 --> 00:04:17.000
quickly.

00:04:17.340 --> 00:04:19.360
"Listen, I'm just setting the plan.

00:04:20.000 --> 00:04:21.900
Tommy's doing the work."

00:04:22.020 --> 00:04:24.600
Hardy's got a lot to live up to, given Venom's
reputation.

00:04:25.120 --> 00:04:29.160
But considering the actor's ability to fully
commit to a role, there should be no doubts.

00:04:29.420 --> 00:04:30.720
Peter Parker, look out.

